Indeed, I believe that allowing the player to apply acidic corpses as a
method of curing petrification would work quite well. Although most, if
not all acidic corpses [that aren't in tins] decay eventually, being
able to apply them many times over while you posess the fresh corpse
would be an appropriate counterbalance to having a single use lizard
corpse that never decays.

Alternatively, it might make more sense to force the player to tin an
acidic corpse, so that it could be used as a sort of salve. Even if
this step was unnecessary in curing stoning by applying an acidic
corpse, it could certainly be used to prolong the viability of said
corpse, as this is already possible in Nethack.



